    "model_answer": "Yes, the documents suggest that NR5A2 is important in the development of endometrial tissues. In Document 3, it is mentioned that Lrh-1 (a factor important for pregnancy) regulates metabolism and hormone synthesis, and reduction of NR5A2 transcript abundance by RNA interference abrogated decidualization in a primary culture of",
    "selected_doc_ids": "[\"1780819\", \"25263942\", \"15928989\"]",
