    "query_text": "Tumor-treating fields are effective for treatment of which cancers?",
    "reference_answer": "Clinical trials have shown that Tumor-treating fields are effective for treatment of non-small cell lung cancer and glioblastoma. Ongoing and future trials will evaluate TTFields in solid tumor brain metastases, and ovarian, pancreatic cancers and multidrug resistance cancer cells.",
    "model_answer": "The provided documents suggest that tumor-treating fields (TTFields) have been approved for the treatment of recurrent glioblastoma and have shown potential efficacy in other solid tumors such as nonsmall cell lung cancer, but there is no direct evidence found in the provided documents about their effectiveness for treatment of cancers other than glioblastoma and non-small cell",
    "selected_doc_ids": "[\"bioasq_18596382\", \"bioasq_24884522\", \"bioasq_23659608\", \"bioasq_25213870\", \"bioasq_23095807\", \"bioasq_23899985\", \"bioasq_23891283\", \"bioasq_24555979\", \"bioasq_19133110\", \"bioasq_21548832\"]",
